         <div class="intro-row">
          <div class="lead">

            <p>
              I am currently a <strong>Senior Researcher at Huawei Research Center in Zürich</strong>,
              working on next-generation <strong>Neural Processing Units (NPUs)</strong>.
              My research interests span computer architecture, compilers,
              and hardware generation.
            </p>

            <p>
              I completed my <strong>Ph.D. in Computer and Communication Sciences at EPFL</strong> in 2026, advised
              by Prof. Paolo Ienne (EPFL) and Prof. Lana Josipović (ETH Zürich).
              My doctoral research brought concepts from
              <strong> out-of-order superscalar processors</strong> into
              <strong> dynamically scheduled high-level synthesis (HLS) </strong>
              to exploit parallelism in dataflow circuits generated from sequential programs.
            </p>

            <p>
              In 2023, I began a <strong>six-month research internship at AMD </strong>
               in Longmont, Colorado, under the supervision of Dr. Kristof Denolf,
              working on architecture-aware scheduling and design space exploration
              for mapping neural networks onto AMD AI Engines.
            </p>

            <p>
              I earned my <strong>B.Sc. in Computer Engineering in 2020</strong> from the
               <strong> American University in Cairo</strong>,
              graduating <strong><em>summa cum laude</em></strong> and started my Ph.D. in the same year.
            </p>

